WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.627
"When will we be out of this forest?" Dorothy asked the Tin Man.

2
00:00:06.628 --> 00:00:11.409
"Oh, I don't know," he replied. "But we are safe.

3
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:16.519
I have my ax and my oilcan. Nothing but fire can hurt the Scarecrow.

4
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.719
And you have the kiss of the Good Witch on your forehead."

5
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.763
"Who will protect Toto?" asked Dorothy nervously.

6
00:00:24.764 --> 00:00:32.557
Suddenly a lion jumped onto the road and made a terrible roar.

7
00:00:32.558 --> 00:00:41.550
With one blow of his paw, the lion sent the Scarecrow spinning, and with another blow, he struck the Tin Man down.

8
00:00:41.551 --> 00:00:44.734
Toto barked and rushed toward the lion.

9
00:00:44.735 --> 00:00:48.482
The lion opened his mouth, and Dorothy was frightened for Toto.

10
00:00:48.483 --> 00:00:51.759
She slapped the lion on his nose as hard as she could.

11
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.306
"Don't you dare bite Toto!" screamed Dorothy.

12
00:00:55.307 --> 00:01:01.874
"You should be ashamed! A big lion like you biting a little dog!"

13
00:01:01.875 --> 00:01:05.516
"I didn't bite him," said the Lion.

14
00:01:05.517 --> 00:01:11.513
"No, but you tried to," said Dorothy. "You're nothing but a big coward."

15
00:01:11.514 --> 00:01:16.214
"Yes," said the Lion, hanging his head in shame.

16
00:01:16.215 --> 00:01:22.593
"I can't help it. I've always been a coward."

17
00:01:22.594 --> 00:01:28.027
"Why are you a coward?" asked Dorothy, looking at the great beast in surprise.

18
00:01:28.028 --> 00:01:30.573
He was as big as a small horse.

19
00:01:30.574 --> 00:01:36.738
"I don't know," he replied. "I guess I was born this way.

20
00:01:36.739 --> 00:01:43.055
I've never had to fight. I've only had to roar."

21
00:01:43.056 --> 00:01:48.635
"That's not right," said the Scarecrow. "A lion should be brave."

22
00:01:48.636 --> 00:01:53.933
"Yes," said the Lion, wiping a tear from his eye with his tail.

23
00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:58.665
"But whenever there is danger, I get scared."

24
00:01:58.666 --> 00:02:02.475
"You just need some courage," said the Tin Man.

25
00:02:02.476 --> 00:02:09.003
"Yes," said the Lion tearfully. "I need courage."

26
00:02:09.004 --> 00:02:12.667
"You should come with us," said Dorothy.

27
00:02:12.668 --> 00:02:15.934
"We're going to see the Wizard," added the Tin Man.

28
00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:19.659
"The Wizard?" asked the Lion.

29
00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.717
"Yes, the Wizard of Oz," explained Dorothy.

30
00:02:23.718 --> 00:02:30.763
"I want to go home; the Scarecrow wants a brain; the Tin Man wants a heart; and you need courage."

31
00:02:30.764 --> 00:02:37.998
"Yes, courage," said the Lion. "I want to ask for courage."

32
00:02:37.999 --> 00:02:42.262
They camped under a large tree near a small stream.

33
00:02:42.263 --> 00:02:46.017
Dorothy and Toto ate the last of their bread.

34
00:02:46.018 --> 00:02:50.720
"Take these," said the Scarecrow, giving Dorothy a handful of nuts.

35
00:02:50.721 --> 00:02:54.271
"If squirrels can eat them, then so can you."

36
00:02:54.272 --> 00:02:58.939
"Oh, thank you," said Dorothy.

37
00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:04.935
After breakfast they set off. While walking, they heard strange noises.

38
00:03:04.936 --> 00:03:06.833
They immediately began to run.

39
00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:09.350
"Did you hear that?" asked Dorothy.

40
00:03:09.351 --> 00:03:13.290
"They are the Khalidahs," said the Lion.

41
00:03:13.291 --> 00:03:16.634
"What are the Khalidahs?" asked Dorothy.

42
00:03:16.635 --> 00:03:23.732
"They are monsters with bodies like bears and heads like tigers," replied the Lion.

43
00:03:23.733 --> 00:03:28.026
"I'm very afraid of them."

44
00:03:28.027 --> 00:03:32.505
Dorothy and the others reached a cliff with a river far below.

45
00:03:32.506 --> 00:03:39.033
"Oh no!" screamed Dorothy. "We're trapped! What will we do now?"

46
00:03:39.034 --> 00:03:42.853
"Here is a tall tree," said the Scarecrow thoughtfully.

47
00:03:42.854 --> 00:03:46.433
"With Tin Man's help, we could make a bridge."

48
00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:54.532
"Excellent idea," said the Lion.

49
00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:58.848
Tin Man cut down the tree so it formed a bridge across the river.

50
00:03:58.849 --> 00:04:02.591
As the group began to cross, they heard a sharp growl.

51
00:04:02.592 --> 00:04:06.527
They all turned to look and saw two Khalidahs running toward them.

52
00:04:06.528 --> 00:04:13.680
"Quick!" cried the Lion.

53
00:04:13.681 --> 00:04:18.152
He roared at the Khalidahs while his friends made it across the bridge.

54
00:04:18.153 --> 00:04:34.309
The Khalidahs stopped but then rushed forward again.

55
00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:41.283
"My roar didn't work!" cried the Lion. "They're still coming!"

56
00:04:41.284 --> 00:04:45.560
"Tin Man, start chopping the bridge!" said the Scarecrow.

57
00:04:45.561 --> 00:04:49.043
"Yes," said Dorothy, "and hurry!"

58
00:04:49.044 --> 00:04:52.655
Right away the Tin Man swung his ax at the bridge.

59
00:04:52.656 --> 00:04:58.664
The bridge soon collapsed, carrying the ugly beasts with it into the river below.

60
00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:02.400
"You were so brave," Dorothy said to the Lion.

61
00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:07.626
"No, I was so scared," said the Lion.

62
00:05:07.627 --> 00:05:11.754
"Anyway, we made it," said Dorothy, relieved.

63
00:05:11.755 --> 00:05:16.518
"Yes, and look," said the Tin Man. "We're almost out of the forest."

64
00:05:16.519 --> 00:05:22.355
"To the Emerald City!" said Dorothy.

